From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] linux-dmabuf-v1: send the explicit LINEAR modifier to v3
 clients

wlroots collapses a format whose modifier set is exactly {LINEAR,
INVALID} to INVALID-only in the v3 modifier events, as a workaround for
XWayland passing unfiltered modifier lists to GBM
(https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/issues/1166).

On this device that set is EVERY format: mesa/freedreno on a5xx reports
exactly one explicit modifier (LINEAR) for all 64 formats, so the
workaround strips the explicit modifier from the entire list, for every
v3 client, not just XWayland. GStreamer's waylandsink (>= 1.24, still
true in 1.28.5) then drops INVALID by policy in its dmabuf_modifier
handler, is left with an empty drm-format list, and silently falls back
to CPU-converting 1080p video at 4-5 fps where zero-copy runs at 60
(gstwldisplay.c: "we prefer disabling zero-copy over risking a bad
output").

The workaround does not protect anything here: xserver#1166 is about
GBM stacks without modifier support, and freedreno's GBM on this device
imports/creates LINEAR with explicit modifiers correctly (verified with
eglQueryDmaBufModifiersEXT on the GBM, device and surfaceless
platforms). Drop the special case and send the real list; INVALID is
still in the set, so implicit-modifier clients lose nothing.

Upstream-bound: wlroots should gate this workaround on the thing it
actually fears (a GBM without modifier support) instead of erasing
explicit LINEAR for every client of every LINEAR-only GPU.
---
--- a/subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c
+++ b/subprojects/wlroots-0.20.x/types/wlr_linux_dmabuf_v1.c
@@ -800,16 +800,6 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	// In case only INVALID and LINEAR are advertised, send INVALID only due to XWayland:
-	// https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/issues/1166
-	if (fmt->len == 2 && wlr_drm_format_has(fmt, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID)
-			&& wlr_drm_format_has(fmt, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR)) {
-		uint64_t mod = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID;
-		zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_send_modifier(resource, fmt->format,
-			mod >> 32, mod & 0xFFFFFFFF);
-		return;
-	}
-
 	for (size_t i = 0; i < fmt->len; i++) {
 		uint64_t mod = fmt->modifiers[i];
 		zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_send_modifier(resource, fmt->format,
